       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Maximum daily dose:** The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Many references use 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** Single doses are usually capped at 850 to 1,000 mg. A 1,700 mg dose is well above that.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the max for IR.\n- **1,700 mg total per day:** for example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose:** a different dose or frequency.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
