       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem, and I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note.\n\nMetformin has no established benefit above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. A dose of 5,100 mg/day mainly adds risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and a specialist recommendation wouldn't explain it. A transcription or unit error is more likely, such as 1700 mg total per day, or 850 mg three times daily.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range:** for example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose you choose.\n- **Hold the order for review:** you can ask the specialist to re-confirm the dose directly, or contact the pharmacist, who can verify it and override it through the proper channel if it's truly intended.\n- **Consider other options:** if standard dosing failed, the specialist may mean adding or switching to another agent rather than raising metformin.\n\nIf you'd like me to enter one of the in-range doses, tell me which."
      }
     ],
